<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms buy 22,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms buy 22,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd bought a total of 22,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat from Japanese trading house Mitsubishi Corp, traders said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Cheiljedang bought 9,000 tonnes at basis over May futures on the U.S grain futures markets including the Chicago Board of Trade, traders said. Shipment was set for March 10-April 10 to the south eastern port city of Pusan.</p>
<p>Dongah Flour bought the remaining 13,000 tonnes at flat purchase prices.</p>
<p>Details for the results are as follows:</p>
<p>Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Tonne(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		5,000   $153.70</p>
<p>(protein max 10.0%)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  500   $152.20</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 5,300   $179.20</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  2,200   $180.80</p>
<p>Cheiljedang Corp</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Bushel(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		2,500   $0.5475 (over CBOT's May)</p>
<p>(protein max 10.0%)</p>
<p>  Soft White		1,000   $0.5075 (over CBOT's May)</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 2,500   $1.1125 (over KCBT's May)</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  3,000   $1.1825 (over MGE's May)</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
